      "writtenOn": "2022-10-21T13:42:01Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Agreed that it\u0027s getting confusing. The reason for doing it was DRY (single point of `reboot`) and avoid having too many non-`reboot`ing `if` (e.g. for clean-up before `jump_to_payload`), which would be equally confusing and potential sources of bugs ... but I now see that what I actually wanted was `return`!\n\nSo I\u0027ve introduced better abstraction scopes in aosp/2265426 and now `return` on error.",
      "parentUuid": "80063430_5c94d605",
